# PHPUnit caches (the suite added in this change writes these)
/.phpunit.cache/
.phpunit.result.cache

# Composer dependencies. A single rule, matching every other plugin in the
# suite. This rule was already here; beneath it sat 3,626 lines enumerating
# individual vendor paths, every one of them redundant because the directory
# rule above already covered them. Removed rather than maintained — Reach hit
# the failure mode an enumeration invites, where files not on the list slip
# through and get committed.
/vendor/

/build/

# JetBrains IDE files
.idea/

# PHPStan
# phpstan.neon (no .dist) is a local override that wins over the committed
# phpstan.neon.dist outright — PHPStan takes the first file it finds and does
# not merge them. Ignored so a personal tweak cannot be committed by accident.
/phpstan.neon

# composer.lock is COMMITTED, deliberately - do not add it here.
#
# It was ignored across the whole suite until 2026-08-02. That made CI
# resolve dependencies afresh on every run, so the tool versions a build
# used were whatever had been published that morning, and Dependabot could
# only see releases falling outside the composer.json constraints. A
# PHPStan patch that broke the committed baseline was invisible to both.
